    "end": "8591",
    "translation": "Koryak Texts",
    "notes": "Stable markdown line range generated from canonical text."
  },
  "canonical_text": {
    "quote": "",
    "summary": "A Koryak-English vocabulary list giving Koryak terms, Chukchee cognates, and English glosses. Entries include words for water, brandy ('bad water'), goodness and improving weather, a good girl, fire, fire-drill, firelock, 'to get fire', Russians (literally 'fire-tools'), tears and brushing away tears, rain and flooding with water, blood and forcing blood into the face, caravans of pack-sledges and pack-reindeer, doors, coming and following roads or rivers, dried fish and drying-poles, kinship terms such as 'daddy' and 'step-father', fox, and an entry for 'root, also Root-Man', linked to the point where the root and trunk of a tree diverge. Verbs for creating, boasting, desiring, deceiving, squealing, moving, trampling, and working skilfully also appear.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The term 'mi'mil' is glossed as 'water', with related forms for 'having water'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The compound 'aqa'-mi'mil' is glossed as 'brandy (literally, bad water)'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The form 'gi'mlilin' is glossed as 'having water'.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "The personal name 'Miti'' is glossed as 'the name of Big-Raven's wife'.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "Big-Raven is mentioned indirectly as the husband of Miti, whose name is defined as 'Big-Raven's wife'.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "The word 'mi'jhin' is glossed 'fire', with related entries for a fire-drill, a firelock, and a verb meaning 'to get fire'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "The term 'me'lhi-ta'n-nitan' and the stem 'milh-' are glossed 'Russian', with a note that the literal meaning is 'fire-tools'.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The word 'mu'Limul' is glossed as 'blood'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "The verb forms 'muLita'wikm' and 'muLite'witkm' are glossed as 'to force blood (into the face)'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "The noun 'mu'qamuq' is glossed as 'rain'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Verb forms 'muqaiu'ykm' and 'muqa'tiykm' are glossed as 'the rain comes' and 'it rains'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "The verb 'ta'ykm' is glossed 'to flood something, to cover something with water'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The terms 'ta'mkal', 'tai'nat', and 'ta'waj' are glossed respectively as 'drying-pole, a set of drying-poles', 'food, dried fish (chiefly dog-salmon)', and 'dried salmon'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "The entry 'ta'tkan, tatka'gitnm' is glossed as 'root, also Root-Man', with a Chukchee cognate glossed as 'point of divergence of root and trunk of tree'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "The gloss 'root, also Root-Man' indicates that 'Root-Man' is a named figure associated with the root of a tree.",
      "category": "other",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "The word 'ti'utiL' is glossed as 'door'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "The terms 'ta'ta' and 'tata'thilan' are glossed as 'daddy' and 'step-father'.",
      "category": "relationship",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "The entry 'ta'tol Pal., yayol K' is glossed as 'fox'.",
      "category": "object",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "Forms based on 'muu-' and 'mgu-' are glossed as belonging to a caravan of pack-sledges, to move on with pack-sledges, pack-reindeer, pack-sledge road, and line of pack-sledges.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "The forms 'nitami'nnaqin' and 'taminna'tekin' are glossed as 'he is skilful, he is a handicraftsman' and 'to work skilfully'.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:21",
      "text": "The verb 'mala'tikin' is glossed 'it grows better (the weather)' and 'mahtva'tikm' as 'to make the weather better'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:22",
      "text": "The verb 'tai'kikm' is glossed 'to make, to create'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:23",
      "text": "The verb 'tayili'fiikm' is glossed as 'to grope in the dark', and the phrases 'qai-ta'yicina' and 'qai-ca'yicina' are glossed 'groping slowly'.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:15"
      ]
    }
  ],
