      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "The vocabulary distinguishes 'outside' (ga'cnm, na'cnm) from 'world' (ila'cnmen), both given with Chukchi cognates.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "There is a noun nai'nai glossed 'mountain' with a Chukchi cognate.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "The morpheme -ftaw- denotes 'woman, female (only in composition)' and forms compounds for old woman, female thief, daughter (literally 'female son'), she-dog, wife, generic 'woman', and female cousin.",
